{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nint n, cnt[256], id[256];\nint prob[10][256];\nvector<int> groups[10];\nmap<long long, int> cache;\n\nint fastpow(int a, int b) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) res = (long long)res * a % MOD;\n        a = (long long)a * a % MOD;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint solve(int level, long long mask) {\n    if (mask == 0) return 0;\n    if (level == n) return 1;\n    long long key = ((long long)level << 50) | mask; // combine\n    auto it = cache.find(key);\n    if (it != cache.end()) return it->second;\n    int total = 0;\n    for (int subset = 1; subset < (1 << n); ++subset) {\n        long long next_mask = 0;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < (int)groups[level].size(); ++idx) {\n            if (!(mask & (1LL << idx))) continue;\n            int val = groups[level][idx];\n            for (int b = 0; b < n; ++b) {\n                if ((subset & (1 << b)) && !(val & (1 << b)))\n                    next_mask |= 1LL << id[val | (1 << b)];\n            }\n        }\n        total = (total + (long long)prob[level][subset] * solve(level + 1, next_mask)) % MOD;\n    }\n    cache[key] = total;\n    return total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n    cin >> n;\n    int inv100 = fastpow(100, MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        prob[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int x;\n            cin >> x;\n            int p1 = (long long)x * inv100 % MOD;\n            int p0 = (MOD + 1 - p1) % MOD;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); ++k) {\n                prob[i][k | (1 << j)] = (long long)prob[i][k] * p1 % MOD;\n                prob[i][k] = (long long)prob[i][k] * p0 % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i)\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i >> 1] + (i & 1);\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        groups[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = (int)groups[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    cout << solve(0, 1) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef main():\n    data = list(map(int, sys.stdin.read().split()))\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = next(it)\n    inv100 = pow(100, MOD - 2, MOD)\n\n    # prob[level][subset] = probability for that level and subset\n    prob = [[0] * (1 << n) for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        prob[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(n):\n            x = next(it)\n            p1 = x * inv100 % MOD\n            p0 = (MOD + 1 - p1) % MOD\n            for k in range(1 << j):\n                prob[i][k | (1 << j)] = prob[i][k] * p1 % MOD\n                prob[i][k] = prob[i][k] * p0 % MOD\n\n    # popcount for all masks\n    cnt = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i >> 1] + (i & 1)\n\n    # groups by popcount, and id mapping\n    groups = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    id_ = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        c = cnt[i]\n        groups[c].append(i)\n        id_[i] = len(groups[c]) - 1\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def solve(level, mask):\n        if mask == 0:\n            return 0\n        if level == n:\n            return 1\n        total = 0\n        for subset in range(1, 1 << n):\n            next_mask = 0\n            for idx in range(len(groups[level])):\n                if mask & (1 << idx):\n                    val = groups[level][idx]\n                    for b in range(n):\n                        if (subset >> b) & 1 and not ((val >> b) & 1):\n                            new_val = val | (1 << b)\n                            next_mask |= 1 << id_[new_val]\n            total = (total + prob[level][subset] * solve(level + 1, next_mask)) % MOD\n        return total\n\n    print(solve(0, 1))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016008525562938303, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002650863316375762, -0.00028975578607060015, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.01105375587940216, -0.023804696276783943, -5.9602869441732764e-05, 0.0, -1.0132738680113107e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -7.867782187531702e-06, -5.864924969500862e-05, -2.1457441107486375e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00012575789878610522, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -0.0002097863471135497, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -0.2852599024772644, -0.011049983091652393, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00010084597306558862, 0.0, -0.5763612985610962, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.156323378381785e-05, 0.0, -0.02324567921459675, -2.50339189733495e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.4768567681312561, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -7.867782187531702e-06, -1.4066597032069694e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, 0.0, -0.12695272266864777, -0.07889184355735779, -0.000457063142